{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge","id":589556,"title":"Let's Talk About The Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-13T14:44:06-07:00","id":589556,"title":"Let's Talk About The Hedge","content":"This is not an essay. Sorry if you're still waiting on that, it's coming.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I still wanted to start the conversation on the Hedge. We've gotten really focused on the splats between Seemings, Courts, Kiths, and such, so I wanted to draw back and talk about the world spaces, and I want to start off with the Hedge rather than dreams because I fucking love the Hedge.<br /> <br /> So, let's kick off with the easiest question to kick up crap with: <b>What has been the hardest part of using the Hedge in your stories and games?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:48:51-07:00","id":589580,"title":"","content":"Making the notion of using it for more than just the strictly necessary seem tempting rather than unthinkable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:53:37-07:00","id":589583,"title":"","content":"When you have time, could you expand on that a little? I know what you're talking about, but I want to explore it a little through your experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:54:21-07:00","id":589584,"title":"","content":"If I'm being completely honest, it's the question of how consistent the Hedge is nearer to the mortal world/in a given area, particularly in the areas neighboring trods and/or Hollows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:56:46-07:00","id":589585,"title":"","content":"I know there was a concept of Trods as well travelled roads in the very early book, and that's not what quite you were talking about, but that reminds me, did they ever expand on that idea or did it disappear entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T15:05:30-07:00","id":589589,"title":"","content":"How and where it's populated. It's supposed to be just paths bordered by thorns, but you can also go into the thorns, and apparently changelings do on their escape from Arcadia, but there's also goblin markets, and hobgoblin populaces. Do they just line up on the side of the road? Or is there a big wide open area?<br /> <br /> Also, since you can open a portal to the Hedge anywhere, a good way to figure out where it deposits those who do. If I walk down a hallway opening doors and portals to the Hedge, are they opening up on the other end right next to each other, alongside a corresponding corridor in the Hedge? Or are they popping out all over the Hedge, conceivably thousands of miles apart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-13-2015, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T15:19:13-07:00","id":589596,"title":"","content":"If anything, that's the primary aspect of trods that's stuck around; a quick skim of my library turns up &quot;trods&quot; almost exclusively as some variant of &quot;consistent pathway through the Hedge,&quot; whereas &quot;place of power&quot; has in practical terms fallen by the wayside save for its indirect sense of &quot;a lot of changelings use trods as steady ground to set up horticultural Glamour supply posts.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I must also note that, despite my signature, my readthrough of the line's been half-suspended at Lords of Summer since mid-May; keeping up with Mummy and Beast diverted my attention about as much as work and family obligations and more frequently-updated media, all of which has finally died down enough that I can pick things up again.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-13-2015, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:44:21-07:00","id":589775,"title":"","content":"The Hedge, yeah... That's a lot in terms of a 'friendly discussion' sort of thing. I'll try to keep my comments on point, but I have some thoughts that are less-than-productive when I apply my mind to what I've seen about Second Edition. Sorry in advance if I sound like a tosser.<br /> <br /> My biggest joy about using the Hedge in a game is also my biggest worry. That is, how I describe it to players always feels right on the edge of saying too much and not saying enough. I don't want to ever say, 'Remember the movie <i>Labyrinth</i>? Yeah, that's it...' BUT I also want to give my players a real feel for what the Hedge is like. The 'psychoactive' properties of the Hedge make it possible\u2014at least at MY table\u2014for the Hedge to look, feel, smell, generally present itself in slightly different ways to different observers. I try to give broad-strokes descriptions of various Hedge locales and allow players to fill in the blanks. But then there's the whole notion of the Hedge reflecting the 'real world' around it.<br /> <br /> Our first chronicle was set in New York City, and I wanted to allow the Hedge to reflect some part of the Big Apple. I never quite felt like I'd done that effectively, no matter what the players in our troupe thought. So, does the Manhattan skyline appear above the Hedge in Central Park? Can the plucky Darkling from Jersey hear traffic from the Lower East Side when she's stalking a hobgoblin? Does the stink of garbage or the perfume of cherry blossoms make it through the Thorns? My take on all of those was to lean on that same 'psychoactive' nature of the Hedge as justification to just let it do what-the-hell-ever I needed for the scene.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's what the Hedge is there for, I dunno. It's not a PLACE really, but it feels like a place. The Hedge isn't alive and sentient, but it reacts to moods and desires, even going so far as to trick the unwary sod who enters its borders. It's not a part of Faerie, but the Others can survive there and command the Thorns in ways changelings cannot do. It's all kinds of possible.<br /> <br /> My reason for posting here is that I wonder if anyone else uses the Hedge like that. I remember thinking long and hard about the whole notion of the Hedge from the first book for <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> that I saw\u2014<i>Autumn Nightmares</i>, if you need to know\u2014and it straight up preyed on my mind for weeks. When I actually read it, I was delighted to see how the <b>Changeling</b> core book\u2014and subsequent books\u2014dealt with the Hedge by offering <i>direction</i> without mandating onerous mechanics. All I'll say here about my hopes for Second Edition is that I do not want to lose that freedom to make the Hedge whatever works in my game. I mean, I KNOW that I'll keep doing that, but I want others to feel like they can do too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T00:49:42-07:00","id":590019,"title":"","content":"I'd say the two hardest parts for me are:<br /> <br /> 1) How the rolls fit togeather. For example, there's Clarity roles and there's Wits + Survival rolls. What does each one do, and how do they fit togeather as part of navigating the hedge.<br /> <br /> 2) Can or can't two places in the hedge be &quot;close&quot; in any meingful sense (without Trods involved) and if so how does that work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T01:22:33-07:00","id":590020,"title":"","content":"For me, hardest was nature of hedge. Just...what the hell should I portray it as? Veil between Arcadia and Earth? It's own dimension, sibling to Arcadia? Something inbetween? Reflection of mortal world, changed by power of Faerie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T05:33:56-07:00","id":590162,"title":"","content":"The hardest part for me is to convince players to go there, to a place in which each possible location is a deathtrap, obvious or not, and where every critter is out there to get you, eat you, enslave you, or worse. And that without counting a Gentry encounter. <br /> Why don't simply keep yourself tending your private hollow, growing goblin fruits or performing oneiromancy, with your wards keeping the danger out? <br /> I think Second Ed. should make the trips to the Hedge more tempting and rewarding, and the Hobs a bit more ambivalent to the changeling travellers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-14-2015, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T12:49:17-07:00","id":590407,"title":"","content":"I've always looked at the Hedge as a Pseudo-Dream Subspace. Where eternal emotions and thoughts of dreams merge and combine with a mortal realm foundation. Always twisting and changing for the &quot;Dreamer&quot; or &quot;Traveler&quot; yet keeping some general elements to itself. Hardest part for my group is always wondering how it looks each time we go in.<br /> <br /> I considered the entrance to each &quot;Door&quot; would reflect the Hedge area you pass through. A semblance of the mortal area you leave before you go in. (Ex: Going through a garden will lead to a bizarre luxurious garden, Diving into a pool after you come up, to see a beach full of bright white sand that sparkle like bits of diamond over a alien sky or turning down a city alley would lead you to a desolate metropolis or a peculiar shantytown.) Different area's to pass through, different dangers to face and even if you go through the same gate, doesn't mean the dangers will be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T16:20:41-07:00","id":590569,"title":"","content":"The hardest part for me is really just getting a sense of what the Hedge <i>looks</i> like and conveying that to the players. Just some more illustrations would help. How wide is the path, or is there always a clear path? Can you see over the Thorns? Can you see the sky? Are there structures? Is it like walking in a corn maze (midwesterner, sorry) or a relatively open forest or what?<br /> <br /> I haven't thought about this one in a while, but I remember being really confused by a statement in the core book along the lines of &quot;you become lost in the Hedge if you lose sight of the mortal world.&quot; I don't understand how you would be able to see the mortal world from the Hedge in the first place and when exactly you would lose sight of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T21:36:34-07:00","id":590832,"title":"","content":"For the record, I have some thoughts on stuff brought up, I just don't have time to get them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T01:07:50-07:00","id":591015,"title":"","content":"Hardest thing? Hmmm. One of the issues that I've come across with using the hedge is more of a reflection on the Storyteller. Sometimes the hedge gets presented in a way that 'If you go here, you're screwed'. Having the hedge show up as 'This is a tool that you Changelings can use... but just like any tool, you have to use it properly or else you're going to cut yourself. You already have had some success with it; you escaped from Arcadia, after all. So now you have to learn to use it properly. There's good stuff here, and there's bad stuff here. I can show you how to be safe here... and when you're ready, I can show you how to not be as safe, and why you might want it to be that way.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T08:25:10-07:00","id":591356,"title":"","content":"1. As far as the &quot;getting them to go there&quot; part goes, I recommend leading by example. Have some middle ranking characters in the freehold (e.g. not the heads of the Courts, but with more status than the players) ask for some assistance/body guards while they proceed on hedge business. Maybe they gather goblin fruits for the feast at the next big gathering at the Commons, or maybe the king wants to make sure the trods haven't shifted locations since last time they were checked, or maybe the freehold frequently patrols the Hedge near the mortal world for signs of Gentry and to keep dangerous Goblins out of the area. Along the way you can have them point out locales not to enter and which roads are &quot;most often&quot; safe to travel down. Let the veterans spin a few stories about how they narrowly escaped from their rivals by popping into the Hedge, or how they used the trods to sneak into a bank after closing time. Illustrate how it can be both dangerous and useful.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm lucky in that I have a highly wooded park near my house. Lots of trails, and I've sometimes gotten lost exploring them. If you want a feel for the Hedge, try to find places like that in your area. <br /> <br /> 3. I like to assume that Hedge gates close to the mortal world reflect something of the near side. For instance, a gate leading into a library in the mundane world is filled with bookcases (full of books containing gibberish or tokens of forbidden knowledge) forming a maze on stony ground with long thorny vines growing over the stacks and the sky open overhead. Other places might look like a junk yard. I like to assume that the Hedge has a taste for lost things, so many of the signs of humanity are indeed objects sucked into the Hedge (insert joke about socks missing in the laundry here). Occasionally sounds intrude from the mortal world...given the timey whimey nature of them a changeling can't ever be certain if the sounds or whispers are from the past, present or future. Occasionally if you listen hard enough you might hear some snatch of conversation pertinent to your interests...or the screams of someone you care about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:53:29-07:00","id":591606,"title":"","content":"A few bits of advice for dealing with Goblins:<br /> <br /> 1. Goblins are strange, and they only get stranger. The ones lurking near the human world tend to at least have somewhat comprehensible goals. They are either things and people from that world who slipped inside the Hedge and became something else, or things born in alien realms who have reason to linger close to humanity. Do not mistake them for benign goals. Some of them simply have a love of humans, or human dreams, or human things. Some like to hoard mundane treasures, perhaps sneaking into the human world with this in mind. Others have an appetite for human flesh (or other creatures from the mundane world...but human flesh is often a safe bet as these things go). Others work for the Market, or trade in the Market, or beg at the Market...or are sold by the Market. None too few make a decent trade by kidnapping humans and changelings to sell to Arcadia. The point is...whatever they are, they are often the most reasonable. Go further in and their goals and cares are less centered on the real (ergo, understandable) world. Here a goblin troop might try to catch a rainbow in its nets to sup on juicy colors, or stand unmoving in a living chess game two Gentry began a century ago. <br /> <br /> 2. Mind your manners. If a Gob says good morning, respond in kind. Please and thank you are key. This doesn't mean you should reveal yourself to a Briar Wolf or a Harvest Man. But if one does catch you, do pay it a compliment on a successful hunt. It might save your life. Goblins by and large are vein and egotistical. The Gentry tend to treat them with disdain. There a bit of bitterness inside every Goblin, and what they will not stand for is to be treated that way by a human or a changeling (with the clear exception of Entitlements and Courtly Monarchs). A goblin might still be dangerously no matter how you act, but even one inclined to be civil can turn horribly deadly and maliciously cunning if it takes offense. Etiquette is king, and you insult a Goblin at your own risk. They all have long memories. One final warning, don't expect the Goblin to return the favor. Gobs can and will hurl all manner of abuse at changelings. Don't let it get to you- they relish the chance to treat others as the Gentry treat them. <br /> <br /> 3. Goblins cannot be trusted. Never tell yourself otherwise. Tell them as little about yourself as possible while remaining civil. Do not turn your back on them. Be prepared to defend yourself at any point. Even ones that do you a good turn are best thought of as illicit business partners, willing to work with you for mutual gain but likely to abandon you the moment things get difficult. This rule goes even as you abide by the second rule. In the mind of the Hobs life is cheap. Attempted murder is not a breach of etiquette (although when the fighting is done they might expect an apology from you...be it for wounding them or getting blood on their lovely floor). Goblins lie frequently, and their 'gifts' are as often traps as presents. Refuse (politely) their invitations and offerings unless you have special knowledge about that particular Goblin. <br /> <br /> 4. Listen closely. Ask a Goblin a question and you might hear a lie, a riddle, gibberish, or a real answer. Speak when spoken to and you might hear something useful. Goblins have a habit of talking amongst themselves or speaking their thoughts aloud. Their attentions can drift far when their guests (or prisoners) become innocuous, and none too few like to hold conversations with themselves (or speak their thoughts in poems, rhymes, or songs for that matter). <br /> <br /> 5. Give simple aid. Goblins frequently have strange but simple goals, and any bit of information or middling trinket that might hasten the completion of that goal is welcome. Remember rule 3, of course. The simpler your assistance can be the better. If possible, simply offer that one nail it needs to finish its house or a sprig of wine to dull the sting it suffered from a Hedgebeast. Labor should be offered only to the Gobs you understand the best or the most desperate situations (&quot;My, the fire in your cooking pot looks dim. Perhaps I can collect some wood before I go into the stew?). Goblins are rarely loyal or truly friends of changelings, mind you, but they tend to treat those who do them service better than those who do not (on the simple logic that one who has done them a favor once is more likely to do so again if the Gob is on its best behavior). And even the most pragmatic of Hedge things understand that the Wyrd tends to favor or ignore those who return kindness with kindness, and damns those who do not (not always, mind you, but why tempt literal Fate?). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:57:15-07:00","id":594071,"title":"","content":"On The trouble of getting players in the Hedge:<br /> <br /> It's tough, getting this niche of the archetype just right. I hear you and this is kind of my explanation why.<br /> <br /> See, the thing of the matter is that if there's an overarching motif to this sort of thing, it's that of &quot;Only the foolish go into the woods&quot;. It is the nigh-omnipresent idea put up in fairy tales. Here within our horizon, we know our ways and our laws, but in those woods of the horizon, everything changes. It's not a secret, the Hedge is the woods, and the woods are the wide world, exotic America and foreign Ukraine. It's Araby and the Misty Mountains around Everest and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> And almost without fail, the first person to go into the woods is always a fool. The first sister from Goblin Market, the grandmother from Red Riding Hood (Why is she out in the middle of nowhere with no way to defend herself from the wild?) as well as Little Red herself, the father in Beauty and the Beast-lots of people go out into the world unprepared for it. And the fae? They take advantage of it.<br /> <br /> The second ones to go might be better equipped, but they the ones who would have kept the rule in the first place, who would have stayed in the realm between the horizons. The second sister knew better than to listen to the goblin men, Belle only left because her father's life depended on it. They know better than to leave and succumb to the goblin mischief that rules those lands. Only the Kindly Ones take to those mad places beyond the borders.<br /> <br /> Which is where Changeling the Lost hits a snarl of perspective, because they <i>are</i> the Kindly Ones.<br /> <br /> This strained balance for changelings narratively and psychologically is weird for them, existing as fae creatures....who are still very humanistically-inclined mentally. By all rights, they belong in the Hedge, they are the strange folk of the world, and have every right to know the ways of the woods and to make it twist to their whim and will. They Belong. Except, they Don't. They're more Frodo, or perhaps more on the nose, Bilbo. They are now the weird things of the world, but their memories tie them to mortality. The narrative of Lost actually places them only being steps ahead of the first fool, playing the role of the second(people who know the rules and can make them work, but are still moved to stay out of the woods), and it's still their lot to be sort of fools for entering the Hedge. The dichotomy of difference between the two is tied into the fear of losing themselves to the tale-the more powerful in the Wyrd you are, the more like Them you are, the more the Hedge <i>does</i> twist to your command. And that's not a dichotomy to ignore, because that sets up the narrative you're players are out to break, the third option between the two.<br /> <br /> But that said, it might pay to break some of the narrative of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> I've been following David's mentions on DnD, and I've been poking around Ryuutama, and it occurs to me that both are games that are all about going into the weird and wild world with glee, and I feel like the first ideas for finding the happy medium is between the old cautionary theme with some of the actuality of both those games. In DnD, you don't have to work hard to draw players into their Hedge environment-they go because that is where the enemies are, because that's where the loot is, where the sights can be seen. Ryuutama dispenses the site based idea and indulges in the idea of travelling the Hedge for the sake of it. Taking a cue of memory from Mage, Warehouse 13's pitch to agents was to indulge in a world of endless wonder that they made safer. They went out into that world and dealt with terrifying and life/sanity threatening stuff on a regular basis, but for the most part, the thrill of experiencing that endless wonder drew them in and kept them going(er, for the most part).<br /> <br /> I feel like the Hedge has the elements of this, particularly when you account for how the psychoactive nature of the Hedge means that person looking for adventure is going to find adventure. The rewards are there, baked in. But in regards to its' presentation, there probably should be some dial fiddling going on with the presentation and tone. The Hedge <i>should</i> be scary. Going into the Hedge should always be an evaluated risk. But it needs to be a risk players are willing to bet on.<br /> <br /> Part of my thoughts on this is the idea of 'idle' challenges here and there. I have a philosophy that players shouldn't enter the Hedge without facing some kind of challenge in their time in there, or at least have some kind of meaningful interaction. But there's no reason these challenges need be life threatening(either fatal or capture). The Hedge is supposed to be a place filled with moral and ethical challenges, because part of it's nature is to shift perspective. Present challenges on the road where there are two outcomes and finding another way around, but those outcomes will affect a character.<br /> <br /> Anyways, this is just stuff I've been thinking on that might help if they came into play with the text on the Hedge. I'm still mulling it over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-17-2015, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T16:01:25-07:00","id":594206,"title":"","content":"Getting player characters into the Hedge has worked best in my experience as having them just taken there for the first time by someone else, almost a reenactment of their original abduction by one of the Others. It's not EXACTLY like that, of course, but part of the challenge of <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> is that players don't automatically know what a character can or ought to do... We don't have the same cultural touchstones for fae folk that we do with, say, vampires or wizards or werewolves, right? The very notion of the Hedge is just <i>WEIRD</i> when presented in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=594071#post594071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the thing of the matter is that if there's an overarching motif to this sort of thing, it's that of &quot;Only the foolish go into the woods&quot;. It is the nigh-omnipresent idea put up in fairy tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the best we have going into a <b>Changeling</b> game, and the Hedge embodies everything scary, wondrous, deadly and just plain weird about the woods of fairy tales. Where *I* run into a conceptual barrier is justifying player characters' going into that place when they already have all kinds of scary, wondrous, deadly and weird options in the 'real' world by dint of being changelings and dealing with what comes along with that state. Why go seeking more of that in a place that isn't our known world?<br /> <br /> In that first chronicle we played, I had the players' characters guided into the society of the Lost by an old changeling whose allegiance lay with his Entitlement called the Jackdaw Regency. I totally made it up as a group who had vowed to shepherd newcomers into the larger society of the Lost, and this bloke introduced the characters\u2014and allowed me to introduce the players\u2014to the marvels and dangers that were now part of their shared world. The Hedge was just a piece of this, but the way it came out in the story allowed both characters and players a point of reference for this place-that-is-not-a-place.<br /> <br /> That point about risk that <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\">ArcaneArts</a></b> mentions is vital to any use of the Hedge, of course, and it's something that I bring up as often as I can. Every time the characters need to visit a goblin market or they are tasked with finding some wonder that only grows in the Thorns, the players always wind up discussing it at some length before heading off. Honestly, I'm not sure HOW I instilled this in them, but I'm glad for it. There are all kinds of wonders and horrors in there that my players haven't even imagined, for all that they know about the Hedge already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T17:33:20-07:00","id":594282,"title":"","content":"A large part of what can happen is that players should feel like the Hedge is their domain, regardless of how true that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-17-2015, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:06:20-07:00","id":594820,"title":"","content":"My previous post wound up truncated because I ran out of time at work... Posting on forum boards between library calls isn't always the best idea. Anyway, I think that I was working towards an idea similar to this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=594282#post594282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A large part of what can happen is that players should feel like the Hedge is their domain, regardless of how true that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but when it comes to <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>, even what you think is yours ought to remain scary as F#@K on some level. Terms like 'truth' are relative in our world, more so in the World of Darkness, tremendously so when applied to anything to do with the Lost.<br /> <br /> We all find our ways through, and that's the biggest element of <b>Changeling</b> that I love.<br /> <br /> Still on topic, I'd say that I also struggle with how to describe and use goblin markets in the Hedge. The book <i>Goblin Markets</i> is a wonderful resource, as are the chapters in <i>Rites of Spring</i> and <i>Dancers in the Dusk</i>, but I find myself wanting to describe every minutia available in the market, give every shopper and hob a full personality and back story, make every stall a little world in its own right. That's just impossible, and even <i>trying</i> to do so is exhausting.<br /> <br /> I chose to alleviate that stress by offering two shoppes where the players' characters can find most of what they'd want in a goblin market. Each of these places is run by one of a pair of hobs, brothers who are each 'straight where the other is crooked.' Mr Ochre is stooped, chatty, always willing to haggle on prices but more than willing to swindle a customer who isn't very canny. Mr Blinderbaz is tall, reserved, his wares priced clearly and not open to discussion, though he'll happily accept any offer that is ridiculously in his own favour. Between their shoppes is the every accommodating 'Foode Courte' that rounds out as much of the Upper-Mid-Lower-Round Side Manhattan Market as I've currently sketched out.<br /> <br /> I do kinda dread my players wanting to explore the rest of the market, but my philosophy of solid, troupe-style play gave me the opportunity to tell the players this. One of them is currently working on a larger description of their local goblin market\u2014sans the above mentioned shoppes and 'Foode Courte'\u2014which I hope will give the players more buy in AND make my job a little easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:27:49-07:00","id":594830,"title":"","content":"You know what this reading of the Hedge says to me? Holden Caulfield:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J.D. Salinger, The Catcher in the Rye</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cAnyway, I keep picturing all these little kids playing some game in this big field of rye and all. Thousands of little kids, and nobody's around - nobody big, I mean - except me. And I'm standing on the edge of some crazy cliff. What I have to do, I have to catch everybody if they start to go over the cliff - I mean if they're running and they don't look where they're going I have to come out from somewhere and catch them. That's all I do all day. I'd just be the catcher in the rye and all. I know it's crazy, but that's the only thing I'd really like to be.\u201d </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who's the Changeling? Holden, naturally. He knows it's dangerous and insane to go past and accidentally run off the cliff. But he's still standing there, watching out for people about to go into the Hedge, and snagging them before they do. And who're the kids? Mortals.<br /> <br /> I don't think this works more generally (obviously, Changelings gotta go into the Hedge, too, and lots of Changelings don't actually have it together enough to care about more mortals running off, etc., etc.), but it's what came to mind after the back-and-forth between Arc and Phaolan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:28:09-07:00","id":594832,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, don't get me wrong, the Hedge should be scary as fuck. It should be an engine for dredging up intimate fears and worries for the Lost.<br /> <br /> But that established, the catch to this is that if you make it too scary, then it becomes harder to motivate characters(or their players). Now, truth be told, I never had too much trouble with this at my table-every other changeling in the freehold used the Hedge, so it was established pretty early on that it was a place you could work in, and even if you don't like it it, this is where the fae live and work. You want to get things done, you go into the Hedge.<br /> <br /> But going with a more at home parallel, you very rarely see Werewolf fans express doubt about going into the Shadow(their relationship with the Shadow, what says about the characters, and how the players stereoptype what the game is about is a whole 'nother thing). Now granted, they are predators going into something they are bred for, and werewolves as characters are designed to fee like big bad scary mofos. But they live in a literal dog-eat-dog world, where everything can be summed up by predator-prey relationships, and truth be told the Uratha aren't that much better equipped to face down the Shadow than changelings are with the Hedge.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is scary in different ways-it's a different game, so of course that's the case. It's less in in your face. Changelings also have more reason to be afraid of it than werewolves do the Shadow, because of the very nature of the game. And I wouldn't want to sacrifice that. But this game is a game of Beautiful Madness, and part of the confusion the keeps up the fear is that the fae is something players should want to experience as well. The majority don't want to go back, but how many of them struggle with the mixture of fear and desire as they hide in their bed,screaming at themselves, because they remember another bed that was so divine to lie down in, and part of them wants that even if they don't want anything else?<br /> <br /> My point is that, in acknowledgement of the people who have trouble persuading their players to go into the Hedge, it needs to be established that the Hedge is both terrible and beautiful, a playground to make and a cage waiting to happen. It's not a case of one covering the other, it's both. There's no stinger saying &quot;Much to their inevitable regret&quot;. Players should have mixed feelings about the Hedge, not wholly negative.<br /> <br /> That said, I do want to reiterate that I've never actually had this problem at my table. My players recognized the danger, but they've also been able to go in tons of times and feel more or less at home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-18-2015, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:58:24-07:00","id":594862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=594832#post594832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I do want to reiterate that I've never actually had this problem at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true of my table, as well, but I dunno HOW I managed to instill that in my players. The best moment of that 'see the danger but go there anyway' was in a <i>God-Machine Chronicle</i> crossover where the two changeling characters decided that the only escape route was through the Hedge. They worried about entering it only because they didn't know the Hedge at all out in the Hamptons like they did in midtown Manhattan, and they worried because they didn't know what would happen if the vampire with them came along...<br /> <br /> In all honesty, I didn't know, either, and that journey of discovery was a lot of fun for the whole troupe. They made it to the Autumn Court's Depot ex Libris, but afterward we had a long discussion about the possible dangers they could have faced. Like so many things at my table, the players' questions only fed my devious mind, and they got miffed that I didn't share all that I knew\u2014or what they <i>thought</i> I knew. Yeah, I'm all about troupe-style, we're-all-in-this-together play, but I ALSO keep secrets, tell lies, sometimes trick players into making poor decisions. They let me get away with that because they trust me, and they make me pay for it by doing mad things like dragging a vampire into the Hedge!<br /> <br /> In the end, I want the Hedge to remain a mystery on many levels even as it feels 'more or less' like home. That vibe\u2014danger is right behind you, even where you're safe\u2014can exist in other World of Darkness games, but in <b>Changeling</b> it takes on a different dimension when the Others can snatch you out of your bed or trick you into following a dancing will o' the wisp in Faerie. The Hedge remains my favourite vehicle to drive that notion home when I have to do.<br /> <br /> I think that we're on the same page, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\">ArcaneArts</a></b>, and more than that, I'm right <i>chuffed</i> that we seem to READ that same page slightly differently! Again, that's a piece of what I so adore about this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T22:36:43-07:00","id":595398,"title":"","content":"Anyone remember the story of the Glutton? How if you enter anywhere in Miami between river and 19th street you would wind up in a part of the Hedge near his territory? I took that to heart and started making &quot;bright spots&quot;- zones that were more or less benign and usually under the direct protection of powerful Freeholders (the largest being those portions of the city claimed by the four seasonal monarchs) and &quot;dark spots&quot; that led to areas of the Hedge far more dangerous to be in than normal that players were well advised to avoid unless they wanted to encounter something deadly. The rest of the Hedge I described as somewhere between those two, full of risk but also potential gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T09:54:48-07:00","id":608057,"title":"","content":"In honor of the Hedge getting it's own supplement, <b>What do you want to see in that book?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:53:06-07:00","id":608412,"title":"","content":"Really weird shit. Trods that take you physically into the Skein, gates that open into the wrong time period, giant Hollows that at first appear to be the mortal world, until you look closer and see that things are just a little off. Lots of new Hobgoblins and Hedge Beasts. Story hooks. Crossover material would be nice (Endowments made of Goblin Fruit, a Hollow that serves as a Hell for a demon ring, what the Arisen might do with Tokens, etc etc etc). If this is essentially a Hedge version of <i>Book of the Dead</i>, I would be far from disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:30:15-07:00","id":608599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=608057#post608057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In honor of the Hedge getting it's own supplement, <b>What do you want to see in that book?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like more on hobgoblins and their cultures, habits and societies, the natural resources that can be found there, details on the environnement's psychoreactivity and more options to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T20:25:46-07:00","id":608815,"title":"","content":"To nothri: while your guidelines for using hobgoblins are amazing, I do have qualms about making them out to always be backstabbing jerks in the end. Anything that limits story options without a damn good reason is a bad idea. That's how I roll, but you don't have to do it like me.<br /> <br /> As per requested by our resident Fabulous White Mask, I will share my experiences with the Hedge.<br /> <br /> In my main game, I and my friend are sort of co-STs. My PC is from NWOD, her PC is from her homebrewed setting. We mix it up and the results have been more than satisfying. My PC introduced the Hedge into the story as a sort of uncharted omni-road that leads to lots of useful stuff, but he made it extremely clear that going deeper and off the trod is A Very Dumb-Ass Idea. Lo and behold, their first time out of the path, her PC breaks her ankle and they ride the back of a Laughing One in horse form in their desperation. Moments later, they are holding on for dear life as the damn thing goes super sonic through thorns and branches and dumps them in the middle of nowhere. To get back, they promise to help the Stripling Prince (Autumn Nightmares) in his quest to figure out how Hedgespinning works. They do come home, but the game has moved quite far from that encounter, and I have yet to apply consequences for helping that arrogant fox man. Oh, and her PC was attacked by an Enticer (Autumn Nightmares) when she thought it was a real bleeding person and tried to help it, but she kicked its ass. A legged talking oyster hob offered to make her PC the prettiest necklace ever out of one of my PC's eyes (he has lots of them). Her PC vehemently refused, but the hob kept comically missing the point of why she was refusing.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, my PC and her PC have this adorable little gentlemanly Hedge Beast in the form of a crow as an adopted son. They bought him at a Goblin Market, and their relationship is based on actual love. The shop where the crow was stored was safe and humane, if rather drab. The very worst that was happening to the pets was just boredom brought by increased intelligence. And they still go to Suzaro's (Dancers In The Dusk) seafood restaurant from time to time without guns. They are also on good terms with Billy Birch (Dancers In The Dusk).<br /> <br /> So I guess the Hedge in my game doesn't look like the repellent bear-trap-with-a-sandwich that I imagined.<br /> <br /> EDIT: what I want for the 2ed Hedge supplement? Same as espritdecalmar and Anteros said above. But don't forget updated rules for Hedgespinning and when I am even supposed to use the Token Maker Merit. Hedgespun Vehicles need their own sidebar or something. I want my Goblin Wacky Races, damnit! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-30-2015, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T09:53:22-07:00","id":615229,"title":"","content":"Being in the Hedge and all, what about your experiences in your PC having a Hollow there? What kind of stuff can PCs do with a Hollow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:37:40-07:00","id":615462,"title":"","content":"THis is something I want to talk about.<br /> <br /> Easily some of the most fun I had with Changeling when I was playing Noah Pyre was grabbing my GM in between games and having sessions dedicated to Noah building up his Hollow. I'd tell him what I wanted to add on, and we'd break it down into parts, and each session deal with me having to struggle with the odd bits and ends. I had fights with my garden, lots of arguing with merchants, sneaking in and out of computer stores, and of course long treks into the Hedge. Building it tended to become comedy of errors-we have one game where I scrambled over all of Baltimore and the Hedge looking for a screw, and I seriously thought Noah had been cursed, which dovetailed into me having a paranoid run-in with a freeholder and a large misunderstanding.(Truth was, The GM was rolling really poorly for the stocking of every where I went)<br /> <br /> All of this was great, because the character was Dresden-esque in how he didn't realize just how aloof, strange, and powerful he came across. Noah, for me, was defined by the awkward adventures he had builidng his Hollow. For everyone else though, when Noah came into anaffair, he was like a True Fae, making strange decisions, burning anything that fought him to ashes, and genereally not being there a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> More on my thoughts on this later, I gotta jet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T11:04:41-07:00","id":637177,"title":"","content":"So, let's kick up the conversation again: <b>What do you love about the Hedge?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T16:26:31-07:00","id":637512,"title":"","content":"The diversity of creatures, objects and stories that can be found there.<br /> <br /> The goblin markets.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T00:55:12-07:00","id":637759,"title":"","content":"I Love Hollows and Goblin Fruits, and can't wait to see their iterations in 2e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T10:31:53-07:00","id":639279,"title":"","content":"I love it for what it is, Free Land. Just think of the &quot;real&quot; estate value of a shifting dimension of thorns and bitey things. A second Manifest Destiny. Also Hollows and Hedgespinning/Hedgecrafting. I mean you can make a car that runs on the angst of having too much chilli for dinner! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Furthermore, building things and finding/making your own home has always appealed to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:12:11-07:00","id":639927,"title":"","content":"I love it, because it allows me to add some real fantasy type of story and setting in a more mundane looking campaign setting. Where else can you add a circus where the employees are halfling sized rats and some of the wild animals weird hedge beasts and the characters end up negotiating about compensation to the hag-like master of the circus because of the damages they did? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T10:34:07-07:00","id":640427,"title":"","content":"I love it because it emphasizes the assymetry of playing a changeling. The game is about trauma, and as such feelings of helplessness and danger, that's the personal horror, because you are so very outsized by everything... Even the special, secret place you come from. It isnt like Mage where you can plumb the depths or Werewolf where you belong in it just as much as you do the real world. To a point, it isn't even like Hunter, because you aren't keeping a watchful eye on dangers you might be able to prepare yourself for... The only blind spot on the monsters that changelings face is right on the top of their nose, while they are trying to cross their eyes.<br /> <br /> The rules and niceties of the hedge are all going to pale in comparison to the real risk you face when you step onto those twisty paths, when things go wrong, when danger finds you or deals demand more than you can afford because that is the nature of the world you live in as someone touched by Arcadia.<br /> <br /> It's wonderous and tempting and awesome, yeah, but it isn't nice, it isn't fair, and it isnt something you can ignore - I think it adds an amazing amount of pressure and flavor to the gameline, and like a nesting doll, all its nooks and crannies fit perfectly around the more personal shape of the game, the character, and the 'ideal' player-experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T18:06:45-07:00","id":642278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=608815#post608815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To nothri: while your guidelines for using hobgoblins are amazing, I do have qualms about making them out to always be backstabbing jerks in the end. Anything that limits story options without a damn good reason is a bad idea. That's how I roll, but you don't have to do it like me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I probably should have said number 3 has exceptions, and might not even be the rule depending on which part of the Hedge you find yourself in. I meant that rule as more of a &quot;assume the worst until you see the best&quot; sort of thing. A goblin with personal information about you can be a holy terror if it wants to, so don't give up your secrets until experience tells you it can be trusted with them. Likewise, try not to put yourselves in situations that make you vulnerable to them until you know they won't stab you in the back. Finally, remember that like people even nice goblins can snap and become dangerous. The difference is that what sets a goblin off isn't always what humans would consider sane. If your fortunate enough to make friends with a trustworthy Goblin, take pains to learn what might offend it as carefully as possible. The fae rarely provide a list of trigger warnings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T18:32:25-07:00","id":642307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=608057#post608057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In honor of the Hedge getting it's own supplement, <b>What do you want to see in that book?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Crossover rules for stranger destinations. We know for sure that the Underworld connects to the Hedge. I'd like to hear about what such gates are like on both sides. Same for the Shadow, or the alternate earths and times Demon occasionally plays with (according to the main Demon writeup for Seattle those parallel earths can be accessed by the Hedge, which is all kinds of awesome). Pathways into dreams- how they work, where they can be found, etc. Doorways to other worlds....as in, the dark side of the Moon or something similar. <br /> <br /> 2. Indepth discussion of the trods. Are there any signs that a Hedge gate might be near (groves growing out of season, mushrooms growing in strange patterns, electrical power shutting on or off with no apparent cause, people experiencing moments of lost time, animals displaying unexpected behavior, etc). <br /> <br /> 3. How about some defenses against the hedge? We know it can go almost anywhere and that almost anything can become a door. How about some countermeasures? Maybe nailing a horseshoe above a door or wearing my clothes inside out can act as a barrier to doors opening in a certain radius. I guess I'm asking for a &quot;lock&quot; to compliment the &quot;key&quot; into the hedge, rather than a means of entering let's have a method for keeping the door shut. <br /> <br /> 4. How about something along the lines of a Cunning Man or Wise Woman- mundane humans clever enough to survive the rigors of the Hedge? Maybe some Hedge Alchemy of a sort (after all, if you take a dozen goblin fruits, a pint of goats blood, some chopped briarwolf heart, and toss it all into an iron cauldron during the next solistice, it would be incredibly sad if NOTHING happened, ya know? Through trial and error I can see some folks having a whole slew of recipes of useful and terrible effects in their cookbooks).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T04:32:29-07:00","id":642831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=642307#post642307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if you take a dozen goblin fruits, a pint of goats blood, some chopped briarwolf heart, and toss it all into an iron cauldron during the next solistice, it would be incredibly sad if NOTHING happened, ya know? <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Suspiciously-tasty pudding happens. For some of us, that is enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously though. I like #2 as a parallel to WtF2's Hunting Grounds, ways to keep parts of the hedge consistent and full of ideas without taking away their randomness or whimsy. And #3 has potential - hedge-proofing probably increases your bad luck in the human realm, if only because you attract so much attention while looking like a nutbag. Clarity breaks a small price to pay for overall peace-of-mind when, say, opening the door to pay for a pizza or go to the bathroom or something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T11:58:48-07:00","id":643236,"title":"","content":"On the off hand, I feel like if players have gone through the effort to scour the Hedge for twelve kinds of goblin fruit, stole a goat from a farmer or caught one in the wild, risked life and limb to get briarwolf heart, hunted for and scrounged up the cash for or stole an iron cauldron, and bothered doing something with them in some kind of order on the precise date of the solstice, you've had a story/chronicle play out and the result more or less falls outside of the realm where mere mechanics can decently answer for the acts.<br /> <br /> Not to say Hedge Rituals <i>don't</i> have a place in the book. It's Hedgespinning in a different direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-28-2015, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T12:19:20-07:00","id":643249,"title":"","content":"I definitely like this idea. Goblin Recipes - special methods for preparing and combining goblin fruits that produce unique and impressive results. Great fodder for goblin markets. Characters could buy special concoctions, try to steal secret recipes, learn from potions masters or goblin chefs. So much potential!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T12:24:39-07:00","id":643252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=642307#post642307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. How about some defenses against the hedge? We know it can go almost anywhere and that almost anything can become a door. How about some countermeasures? Maybe nailing a horseshoe above a door or wearing my clothes inside out can act as a barrier to doors opening in a certain radius. I guess I'm asking for a &amp;quot;lock&amp;quot; to compliment the &amp;quot;key&amp;quot; into the hedge, rather than a means of entering let's have a method for keeping the door shut. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I especially like this. Had some house rules/homebrew in my old campaigne to this effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T21:48:30-07:00","id":647663,"title":"","content":"The problems with the hedge I've seen in play are that it's basically another dimension but doesn't ever directly reference how that works.<br /> <br /> Is the hedge coterminous? (Does it line up 1:1 with the mortal world)<br /> <br /> The answer is no; it is possible for distance to be meaningless in the hedge, just like in the shadow. You can walk thirty miles in the hedge and be only thirty feet from where you entered on the mortal side.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, doors work differently. A door into the hedge is a Fixed Point. FPS are static, places which exist relative only to each other. If FP 1 is accessed from a certain door, it's always accessed from that door. If FP 2 is thirty minutes hard riding north of FP 1, it is. If FP 3 is forty five minutes hard ride north east of FP 1, it is. But if you think this means FP 2 and FP 3 are thirty minutes hard ride from each other, you're mistaken. Only existing established relationships can be taken as given, and sometimes not even then. The ones that NEVAR change are trods. The ones that sometimes shift are just paths.<br /> <br /> Doors are a little different. They nail the hedge to a certain point on the mortal side \u2013 usually. They always go to the same point \u2013 usually. But it's possible to make one door that opens to multiple places, and is possible to make a door that is a functional portal, so that a changeling with doors 5 in their hollow can have a central portal room that takes them all over the mortal cityscape \u2013 or access several different chunks of hedge, teleporting across intervening distance and having the ability to just run trough the thorns to enter the hedge proper.<br /> <br /> All this is pulled from like, four books, consolidated, and parsed into a whole where the merit for a door or hollow is different in effect from a door or hollow made via RP and where the thorns are dangerous and only paths are safe but the thorns aren't mechanically that bad and paths always exist, and it's entirely possible that none of this is accurate at all.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of the hedge as not behaving in a rational fashion (three locations in a triangle not being arrayed in a triangle; distance being measured in time or danger; &quot;what is known&quot; being as much a law of the place as actual physics is mortal side), but there needs to be a heuristic that players and GMs can grasp and use. I've had to drop out of games because simple conversations about &quot;where are we&quot; led to hours long arguments about this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","user":"SiuiS","date":". 09-01-2015, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","name":"SiuiS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T01:00:42-07:00","id":647764,"title":"","content":"Odd, I never had a problem with that aspect of the Hedge. But maybe I have played enough in earlier games with things like the Umbra or the various coterminous planes in D&amp;D. The border is fixed and coterminous, but as soon as you leave that border area it becomes a different matter. Trods simply immediately leave the border area. The only thing our group sometimes debate about is whether it is save and smart to open a doorway to the hedge at the top of a skyscraper. As of yet, they have never tried it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T01:14:02-07:00","id":647768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge?p=647764#post647764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd, I never had a problem with that aspect of the Hedge. But maybe I have played enough in earlier games with things like the Umbra or the various coterminous planes in D&amp;D. The border is fixed and coterminous, but as soon as you leave that border area it becomes a different matter. Trods simply immediately leave the border area. The only thing our group sometimes debate about is whether it is save and smart to open a doorway to the hedge at the top of a skyscraper. As of yet, they have never tried it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that I've never had a problem with it, either, but others have. Or simply, read less, accepted less as true, or changed things without considering the ramifications. Things snowball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","name":"SiuiS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T01:25:05-08:00","id":783286,"title":"","content":"Apologies for ncero-ing the thread, but there's something I'd really like conveyed in the Hedge and Changeling in general. Storybook whimsy, magic, and logic. I want gates in wardrobes, potions that make you small and cake that makes you tall, poisoned apples, swords in stones, magic beans, talking and walking animals, a house made from a shoe, and the like. Really encapsulate the beautiful madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T17:14:37-08:00","id":783770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/589556-let-s-talk-about-the-hedge#post589556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's kick off with the easiest question to kick up crap with: <b>What has been the hardest part of using the Hedge in your stories and games?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Fear of the Hedge by player and or player characters. Also for me as storyteller getting a good mixture of genuinely rewarding encounters and too good to be true traps was something that took a bit of practice. Initially all encounters were traps and this made the hedge less useful for story purposes. I discovered also it was important to make Hollow truly safe places for their owners, which made the PCs invest in them and then I put plot relevant things in the hollows of NPCs to give the PCs a reason to explore the Hedge, and they knew they should expect a dangerous fortress based on how their own hollow protected them, but they saw this as a challenge, not as a reason to avoid the hedge.<br /> <br /> My hope for the 2ed Hedge is to see various mechanics that use the Lost condition and possibly pull out the whole range of positive and negative condition to paint a picture in beautifully worded mechanics of what it is like in various places in the the hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-10-2015, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}